---
import Journey from '../../layouts/Journey.astro';
import Step from '../../components/journey/Step.astro';
import More from '../../components/journey/More.astro';
import Next from '../../components/journey/Next.astro';
import Fact from '../../components/data/Fact.astro';
import Verified from '../../components/data/Verified.astro';
import CopyPrompt from '../../components/site/CopyPrompt.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/nav';

const ids = ['harnesses.claudeCode.askForEvidence', 't3code.htmlRenders', 't3code.browser'];
const prompt = `When you finish, hand back proof I can judge in a minute, before you say done:
- a screenshot of every page you changed, at phone width (390 pixels) and desktop width
- the test command you ran and its full output
- for any number the change affects: its value before and after
- a short list of what you did not check, and why
If something could not be checked, say so instead of guessing.`;
---
<Journey chapter="proof" first="word" title="Proof you can read" description="An agent can hand back more than the word done: a summary, a test run, a screenshot, a link to try. Each shows you one kind of wrong at a glance.">
  <Step id="word" title="“Done” is one word">
    <p>The <a href={url('journey/check/')}>check from step 5</a> answers yes or no, and here it says yes: one pale puck reaches you with “Done.” and the tray beside you stays empty.</p>
    <p>To know whether the job is what you asked for, you would read every changed line, 212 in this made-up job.</p>
  </Step>
  <Step id="cards" title="Ask for proof with the work">
    <p>Four cards land on the tray one by one: a summary, a test run, a screenshot and a link to try.</p>
    <p>A check says yes or no; a card is something you look at, and each answers one question at a glance.</p>
    <More title="Where this comes from">
      <p><Fact id="harnesses.claudeCode.askForEvidence" show="claim" /></p>
    </More>
  </Step>
  <Step id="catch" title="Each card shows one kind of wrong">
    <p>Six made-up jobs pass the check, four of them not what you asked for, and the card that shows it turns red.</p>
    <p>Switch a card off and its kind of wrong reaches you as “done”.</p>
    <div class="pick">
      <button type="button" data-do="toggle" data-val="sum" aria-pressed="true">Summary</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="toggle" data-val="tests" aria-pressed="true">Test run</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="toggle" data-val="shot" aria-pressed="true">Screenshot</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="toggle" data-val="link" aria-pressed="true">Link</button>
    </div>
    <More title="A worked check for a number">
      <dl>
        <dt>Reference</dt><dd>Fees paid last season, from the club’s own spreadsheet: €14,880 (made-up).</dd>
        <dt>Tolerance</dt><dd>Money: exactly equal. For a measured value, write down how far off is fine before the run.</dd>
        <dt>Rerun</dt><dd>The agent runs it again on a fresh copy of the data and gets the same number.</dd>
        <dt>The card</dt><dd>“Total €14,880.00. Reference €14,880.00. Rerun €14,880.00. Match.”</dd>
      </dl>
    </More>
  </Step>
  <Step id="during" title="Proof while it runs">
    <p>The progress card on the tray grows with each step of a long job, and turns red at step 4, where the agent does something you did not ask for.</p>
    <p>You see it while it works, without stopping it to ask.</p>
    <div class="pick">
      <button type="button" data-do="progress" data-val="on" data-default aria-pressed="true">A progress file</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="progress" data-val="off" aria-pressed="false">Nothing until the end</button>
    </div>
    <More title="In T3 Code">
      <p><Fact id="t3code.htmlRenders" show="claim" /> <Fact id="t3code.browser" show="claim" /></p>
    </More>
  </Step>
  <Step id="ask" title="Say what you want back">
    <p>The cards on the tray change with the work: two screenshots for a page, rows before and after for a script, a failing test that then passes for a fix, with made-up counts.</p>
    <p>Say in the brief which proof you want.</p>
    <div class="pick">
      <button type="button" data-do="kind" data-val="page" data-default aria-pressed="true">A page</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="kind" data-val="script" aria-pressed="false">A script</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="kind" data-val="fix" aria-pressed="false">A bug fix</button>
    </div>
    <More title="A prompt for this">
      <CopyPrompt title="Proof with the work" compact>{prompt}</CopyPrompt>
    </More>
    <Next from="proof" more={[{ href: 'explain/verification/', text: 'Checking the work' }]} />
  </Step>
  <Fragment slot="foot">
    <p>The jobs, the 212 changed lines, the counts and which jobs went wrong are made up.</p>
    <Verified ids={ids} />
  </Fragment>
</Journey>
